{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-9846" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a trigonometry test, the class instructor decided that students whose $z$-score is greater than or equal to $-1$ will pass the test. The mean percent score $x$ of the students of the class is $\\overset{¯}{x}=64.3%$ with a standard deviation of $\\sigma =5.25%.$ Find the minimum passing score." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-9846" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{―}{x}=64.3,$ $z=-1,$ and $\\sigma =5.25$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\  & =64.3+(-1)\\cdot 5.25 \\\\  & =64.3-5.25 \\\\  & =59.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the minimum passing score is $59.05%.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-9846" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad69c954d87f4a299089e3cea60e98a00b5b58cc05c9bf98630b4e721ce1bc52"} {"question" "q-9846" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-9846" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "57.55%"] ["math" "59.05%"] ["math" "61.3%"] ["math" "63.3%"] ["math" "65.3%"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-9846" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "59.05%"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-94478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=28,{x}_{2}=18$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=3.6$ and ${z}_{2}=1.1,$ respectively. Find the mean of the data set." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-94478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}28 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+3.6\\cdot \\sigma .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+1.1\\cdot \\sigma .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(28-18) & =(3.6-1.1)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 10 & =2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this value back into our first equation and solving for $\\overset{¯}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}28 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+3.6\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 28 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+3.6\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\overset{¯}{x} & =13.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-94478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad69c954d87f4a299089e3cea60e98a00b5b58cc05c9bf98630b4e721ce1bc52"} {"question" "q-94478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-94478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10.1"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "12.4"] ["math" "13.6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-94478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13.6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-170510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A data set has a mean $\\overset{¯}{x}=-100$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=-83$ and $z$-score $z=1.7.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-170510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-83,$ $\\overset{¯}{x}=-100,$ and $z=1.7$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -83 & =-100+1.7\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 17 & =1.7\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-170510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad69c954d87f4a299089e3cea60e98a00b5b58cc05c9bf98630b4e721ce1bc52"} {"question" "q-170510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-170510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2.5"] ["math" "7.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-170510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-332054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A data set has a mean $\\overset{―}{x}=-2$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=-1$ and $z$-score $z=1.25.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-332054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1,$ $\\overset{―}{x}=-2,$ and $z=1.25$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -1 & =-2+1.25\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 1 & =1.25\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-332054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad69c954d87f4a299089e3cea60e98a00b5b58cc05c9bf98630b4e721ce1bc52"} {"question" "q-332054" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-332054" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-332274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a certain video game, the mean score of all players is $\\overset{¯}{x}=10$ points with a standard deviation of $1.5$ points. A particular player's $z$-score is $z=2.$ Find this player's score $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38028df82b580d15"} {"question" "q-332274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{―}{x}=10,$ $z=2,$ and $\\sigma =1.5$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ x & =10+2\\cdot 1.5 \\\\ x & =10+3 \\\\ x & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972753/state.json" "file_sha256" "913a86f763ec78c5b411db8d10420ff2679e1ee83e7dd3dc38